6. Later use an unused D item before recap under the actual elapsed-time rule. The order avoids treating helped performance as independent learning.

## Motivation and explanation

A deterministic linear trend shifts expected levels by units perperiod; a linear log trend on positive outcomes models approximately100b1% growth; a quadratic permits curvature. These time forms are substantive choices, not arbitrary polynomial tracking. If the true comparison includesγt but the regression omits it, $u_t=\gamma t+\varepsilon_t$ may be correlated with trendingx. Include the relevant controls or residualise y and every substantivex on exactly the same intercept/time basis and rows. In the full regression, e is orthogonal to1,t,x. Since$x_t=a_x+b_xt+\tilde x_t$ and the residualised columns are orthogonal to1,t, $\sum_t\tilde x_t e_t=0$; summing their equation yields $\widehat\beta=\sum_t\tilde x_t\tilde y_t/\sum_t\tilde x_t^2$ when denominator>0. It is a sample identity, not exogeneity. SSR is the same, but detrendedR² divides by$\sum_t\tilde y_t^2$; fullR² divides by originalTSS. A strong time fit can coexist with weak residualx fit, as in the noted housing example. Full model degrees of freedom remainT−3 for intercept/trend/onex. Exactx trend causes rank failure; perfectly trend-fittedy makes residualR² undefined. Correctly specified deterministic controls address that component, not every persistent process, serial correlation or causal identification.

